From 3e1d3fd24f7537c7ec991f06785b19857d581c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:55:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: t17's draw shaders again, batching in programs of its
 own compiled last; numbered source on a compile failure

t20's one changed vertex shader (the draw program's, with the class select packed into u_dpass)
failed in vitaGL's compiler with no log, and every compile after it failed too (copy and
present, unchanged), so the renderer did not start. The draw program's shaders are t17's again,
compiled first as before. GlGpu::BatchPrograms then builds LayerBatch's vertex shader from
t17's text: a uniform u_sel and, at the end of main, plain nested ifs (no packed uniform, no &&
or nested ?:) that move other classes' triangles outside the clip volume, and compiles it with
the draw and fast fragment shaders, after every other program. If the compiler rejects it,
batching is off (Renderer3D asks GlGpu::BatchOk) and the game draws as t17's native path; the
log says "[gl] batch shader: ok" or "REJECTED ...". THPS_R3D_BATCH=0 doesn't compile them.

A shader that fails to compile is logged with its source, lines numbered.
---
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h          |  22 ++++-
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_shaders_gles.h |  11 +--
 platform/pc/src/pc_gpu_gl.cpp            | 115 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 platform/pc/src/pc_render3d.cpp          |   4 +-
 4 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h b/platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h
index 8f8e065..57735b5 100644
